    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, our offensive core is anchored by the trio of **Seiya Suzuki** (74.37), **Mickey Moniak** (75.98), and **Corbin Carroll** (71.87). **Mickey Moniak** secures the top spot on our board today, buoyed by a significant +14% boost from a favorable platoon advantage against the right-handed McGreevy and a helpful wind-out factor. Similarly, **Seiya Suzuki** is in an elite position against the soft-tossing Dobnak (5.16 xERA), with the wind forecast providing a clear path to production. While **Corbin Carroll** faces a tougher matchup against the left-handed Wrobleski, his elite sprint speed remains our primary weapon in this scarcest of categories; specifically, the opposing pitcher\u2019s slow delivery (85% SB success rate) makes **Corbin Carroll** a prime candidate to steal a bag and single-handedly move the needle for our roster.\n\nThe most difficult roster decision today involved the marginal slot held by **Cole Young** (46.07), who narrowly outlasted **Austin Riley** (43.54). While **Austin Riley** brings a higher historical floor, the optimizer penalized him heavily due to the daunting 2.91 xERA of the opposing starter, Schlittler. Conversely, **Cole Young** benefits from a spot near the top of his order, which provides enough volume to justify the start over the bench option. We continue to monitor the status of **James Wood** and **Giancarlo Stanton**, both of whom remain sidelined on the IL, leaving the heavy lifting to our available core. As we await final lineup cards for **Gabriel Moreno**, **Josh Naylor**, **Brice Turang**, **Max Muncy**, **Travis Bazzana**, **Isaac Paredes**, **Jose Caballero**, and **Tyler Soderstrom**, managers should be prepared to pivot if any of these pieces are scratched, as we have little depth remaining to cover unexpected absences in our hunt for points.",
